[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbf{G}^F$ (the fixed points of a Frobenius endomorphism $F$ on a connected [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mreductive algebraic group $\mathbf{G}$), a maximal torus $T$ of $G$ is $T = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbf{T}^F$ where $\mathbf{T}$ is an $F$-stable maximal torus of $\mathbf{G}$.[0m[38;2;124;124;124mSince $\mathbf{T}$ is a torus (diagonalizable group), it's abelian, and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtherefore $\mathbf{T}^F$ is also abelian.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo yes, $T$ is abelian, $s \in T$, and therefore $T \subseteq C_G(s)$.[0m

